{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZCMdKT96z79zpdeWNWbym","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md\n5\tpredecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\n6\tgeneration: 1\n7\t\n8\t## What this node built\n9\t\n10\tTwo new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns\n11\trepair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):\n12\t\n13\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18\n14\t  (targeted repair planning), D19 (deterministic-vs-model routing), D20\n15\t  (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch).\n16\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator\n17\t  reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +\n18\t  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage\n19\t  predicate N32 will call.\n20\t\n21\tNeither module is registered into the compiled graph yet. `routing.py`'s\n22\tguard tables for D16-D23 already exist (built by N20) and this generation's\n23\tfunctions emit exactly the guard values those tables declare\n24\t(`unit_denominator_passed`/`unit_findings_repairable`,\n25\t`partition_complete`/`convergence_exhausted`, `repair_planned`,\n26\t`model_repair`/`deterministic_repair`, `repair_admitted`,\n27\t`retest_frontier_incomplete`/`retest_frontier_complete`, `unit_accepted`,\n28\t`checkpoint_correlated`) — but `add_node`/`add_conditional_edges` wiring\n29\tthese into `graph.py`'s `StateGraph` is N32's write\n30\t(`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`: N32 owns `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`,\n31\tN31 does not). Every function here is therefore a plain, narrowly-scoped\n32\t`(state, runtime_context) -> update` callable in the same shape N23's\n33\t`model_nodes.py` already uses for D90/D91 — not wrapped in\n34\t`no